{"name":"Blue Hill","hex":"#1e454d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Blue Hill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Hancock County, Maine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Blue_Hill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Hill, Saint Helena","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Hill is one of eight districts of the island of Saint Helena, part of the British Overseas Territory of Saint Helena, Ascension and Tristan da Cunha in the South Atlantic Ocean. It is sparsely populated and comprises the western third of the island. The district is entirely agricultural with no industrial activity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/St_Helena_and_the_Cross_church_in_Blue_Hill.jpg/330px-St_Helena_and_the_Cross_church_in_Blue_Hill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Hill%2C_Saint_Helena","wikidata":"Q4929224"},{"title":"Blue Hill, Kansas","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Hill is a ghost town in Hayes Township, Mitchell County, Kansas, United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Map_of_Mitchell_Co%2C_Ks%2C_USA.png/330px-Map_of_Mitchell_Co%2C_Ks%2C_USA.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Hill%2C_Kansas","wikidata":"Q48848582"},{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill","wikidata":"Q54050"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG/500px-Puijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Puijo Hill in Kuopio, Finland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APuijon_m%C3%A4ki.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/500px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/1280px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg/500px-Bohol_-_Chocolate_Hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate Hills of the Philip